[0m⚙ [0mcompress {"topic":"Preflight review - evidence and analysis","content":[{"startId":"m0001","endId":"m0008","summary":"User asked me (via /tmp/rbx-preflight-review-deepseek.md, m0001) to review a technical preflight for a client-side PWA Roblox classic-clothing editor, with a strict output format (findings + one VERDICT line). I read both docs in full.\n\n## Material read (full contents captured above)\n- `docs/roblox-technical-preflight.md` (316 lines): normative preflight. Claims to lock output dimensions (T-shirt 512x512, shirt/pants 585x559), exact atlas panel rectangles, transform/compositing contract, R15 reference geometry, and a Studio calibration procedure.\n- `docs/roblox-clothing-designer-design.md` (289 lines): overview spec (Preact/Vite/TS/Three.js/fflate, canvas 2D compositor, ZIP projects, Gemini pattern proxy).\n\n## Preflight panel registry (transcribed verbatim, for reference)\nAtlas 585x559, top-left origin, Y-down, half-open rects. 18 panels:\n- Torso: up(231,8,128,64), right(165,74,64,128), front(231,74,128,128), left(361,74,64,128), back(427,74,128,128), down(231,204,128,64)\n- right-limb: up(217,289,64,64), left(19,355,64,128), back(85,355,64,128), right(151,355,64,128), front(217,355,64,128), down(217,485,64,64)\n- left-limb: up(308,289,64,64), front(308,355,64,128), left(374,355,64,128), back(440,355,64,128), right(506,355,64,128), down(308,485,64,64)\nGarment rects (unfolded net, gutters collapsed): torso up(64,0,128,64), right(0,64,64,128), front(64,64,128,128), left(192,64,64,128), back(256,64,128,128), down(64,192,128,64); right-limb up(192,0,64,64), left(0,64,64,128), back(64,64,64,128), right(128,64,64,128), front(192,64,64,128), down(192,192,64,64); left-limb up(0,0,64,64), front(0,64,64,128), left(64,64,64,128), back(128,64,64,128), right(192,64,64,128), down(0,192,64,64). Component extents: torso 384x256, limbs 256x256.\n\n## My verification (performed via arithmetic + web search)\n1. INTERNAL CONSISTENCY of rectangles: VERIFIED CORRECT. All gutters are uniformly 2px (e.g. torso row: right ends x=229, front starts x=231; front ends 359, left starts 361; left ends 425, back starts 427; vertical up ends y=72, front starts 74, etc.). Garment-rect collapse removes exactly one 2px gap per boundary; every garment rect equals atlasRect shifted to component bbox origin minus the accumulated 2px gaps. Up/down caps align over the front face in all three components (e.g. torso up garment x=64 == front x=64). Limb face order (right-limb: left/back/right/front from x=19→217; left-limb: front/left/back/right from x=308→506) is a valid mirror pair and each forms a valid cube unfolding (3 net-continuous edges + 1 cut seam per strip). No missing faces, no off-by-one. Component extents (384x256, 256x256) confirmed by arithmetic.\n2. Panel sizes match public Roblox references: front/back 128x128, torso sides + limb faces 64x128, caps 128x64 (torso) / 64x64 (limbs) — confirmed via generalistprogrammer.com and TikTok/other sources.\n3. T-SHIRT 512x512: CONFIRMED CORRECT against official Roblox doc quote found via web search: 'T-shirts are a square image, such as 512x512 pixels' (create.roblox.com/docs/avatar/classic-clothing). Shirt/pants 585x559 also confirmed ('Roblox only allows 585x559'). Official template ZIP contains only Shirt and Pants templates (T-shirt has no template in ZIP) — consistent with the preflight.\n4. WebGL UV conversion 'atlas pixel edge (x,y) → (x/585, 1 - y/559)' with corner order bottom-left/bottom-right/top-right/top-left: consistent, Y-down→Y-up correct, T-shirt uses 512 denominators.\n5. Transform matrix T(pos)*R*S*T(-cw/2,-ch/2): mathematically correct for center pivot; pattern default positionX/Y=cw/2,ch/2 correctly aligns first tile top-left to component origin at scale 1 (verified by applying matrix to (0,0)).\n\n## Findings I intend to report (draft)\n- IMPORTANT: full-map 'not panel-clipped' (line 135) contradicts 'a panel list clips drawing' (line 146); unresolved whether full-map layers may carry a panel list.\n- MINOR: PreviewFaceBinding.bodyPart is freeform string; R15 torso/limb subdivision (Upper/Lower torso, upper/lower limbs, hands/feet) not expressible/documented; one atlasRect per face.\n- MINOR: 'dimensionless' scale (line 124) actually means dest-px-per-source-px (revealed by full-map formula canvasWidth/cropWidth).\n- MINOR: seams 'reversed' flag semantics undefined (edge direction convention not specified).\n- MINOR: rotation matrix presented as math formula, Canvas API call order not stated.\n- MINOR: design doc line 80 'slightly expanded transparent clothing-overlay meshes' — expansion offset undefined.\n\n## Things I could NOT verify (for Assumptions and gaps)\n- Absolute atlas x/y positions against actual template pixels (did not re-download the pinned ZIP/hashes).\n- FBX UV = body-texture (not 585x559 projection) claim.\n- Claim that orientation matrices are currently identity (no rotation in template faces).\n- Gemini model ID 'gemini-3.1-flash-image' (design doc line 216).\n\nNo blockers identified. Intended verdict: APPROVE WITH CHANGES."}]}
